    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37704" root="لزأ" body-key="l">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَزَأ</span></b>  and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الزأ</span></b> , (K,) or the former only, (TA,)
<i>He filled</i> (K) a water-skin or the like. (TA.) ＝ 
 
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَزَأَهُ</span>, aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَزَاَ</span></b> ; and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لزّأه</span></b> , (K,) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الزأه</span></b> ;
(TA;) <i>He gave him</i> [a thing]. (K, TA.) In
the K, this portion is confused, as well as defective. (TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَزَأَتْ</span> <i>She</i> (a woman) <i>brought forth.</i>
(K.) [You say] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَبَحَ اللّٰهُ أُمًّا لَزَأَتْهُ</span>, (TA,) or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَزَأَتْ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بِهِ</span> (S,) [<i>May God remove far from good,</i> or
<i>prosperity, the mother that brought him forth!</i>] ＝ 
 
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَزَأَ</span>; (K;) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لزّأ</span></b> , (As, S, K,) inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَلْزِئَةٌ</span>;
(As, S;) <i>He tended</i> camels <i>well.</i> (As, S, K.)

